{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"light-sensors","name":"Light and colour sensors","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"A light-dependent resistor module (LDR), a BH1750 light meter (lux, I2C) and a TCS34725 colour sensor (I2C). They see the bench: the room light (the toolbar's Room button), anything held over them, and lit LEDs and screens. Includes BH1750.h and Adafruit_TCS34725.h.","category":"Sensors","needsApp":"0.4.0","code":"// Light and colour sensors. part.light(id).lux is the light reaching an eye (the room's light, shaded\n// by whatever is over it, plus lit LEDs and screens in view); the colour sensor looks with a camera.\n\n// LDR module: the LDR (about 10k at 10 lux, falling as the light grows) over a 10k resistor; the\n// comparator's DO goes HIGH when AO is above the pot's level (darker than the setting).\nbench.device('ldr', (part) => {\n  const eye = part.light('eye');\n  const darkBelow = Number(part.params.threshold ?? 60);\n  const rOf = (lux) => Math.min(1e6, 10000 * Math.pow(Math.max(lux, 0.01) / 10, -0.75));\n  let powered = false, lux = 0, ao = 0, dark = false;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      powered = v >= 2.5;\n      lux = eye.lux;\n      const r = rOf(lux);\n      ao = (v * r) / (r + 10000);\n      const ref = (v * rOf(darkBelow)) / (rOf(darkBelow) + 10000);\n      dark = ao > ref;\n      if (!powered) { io.release('AO'); io.release('DO'); io.draw(0); return; }\n      io.drive('AO', ao, 1);\n      io.drive('DO', dark ? v : 0, 1);\n      io.draw(0.0012 + v / (r + 10000) + (dark ? 0 : 0.002)); // (its DO LED is lit when bright)\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\n      return [`${lux} lux: AO ${ao.toFixed(2)} V, DO ${dark ? 'HIGH (dark)' : 'LOW (bright)'}`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n// BH1750: commands 0x00 power down, 0x01 power on, 0x07 reset, 0x10/0x11 continuous high res,\n// 0x13 continuous low res, 0x20/0x21/0x23 one shot. A read gives 2 bytes: lux * 1.2 (high res).\nbench.device('bh1750', (part) => {\n  const eye = part.light('eye');\n  let powered = false, on = false, mode = 0, lux = 0, reads = 0, addr = 0x23, value = 0, readyAt = 0, now = 0;\n  return {\n    i2c: {\n      address: () => (powered ? addr : -1),\n      write(bytes) {\n        for (const b of bytes) {\n          if (b === 0x00) on = false;\n          else if (b === 0x01) on = true;\n          else if (b === 0x07) value = 0;\n          else if ((b & 0xf0) === 0x10 || (b & 0xf0) === 0x20) { mode = b; on = true; readyAt = now + ((b & 3) === 3 ? 0.016 : 0.12); }\n        }\n        return true;\n      },\n      read(n) {\n        reads++;\n        if (on && now >= readyAt) {\n          const low = (mode & 3) === 3;\n          value = Math.min(65535, Math.round(low ? lux * 1.2 / 4 : lux * 1.2) * (low ? 4 : 1));\n          if ((mode & 0xf0) === 0x20) on = false; // (one shot: sleeps after)\n          if (on) readyAt = now + ((mode & 3) === 3 ? 0.016 : 0.12);\n        }\n        return [value >> 8, value & 255].slice(0, n);\n      },\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      now = io.time;\n      powered = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 2.4;\n      addr = io.level('ADDR') === 1 ? 0x5c : 0x23;\n      lux = eye.lux;\n      io.draw(powered ? (on ? 0.00012 : 0.000001) : 0);\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\n      return [`${lux} lux reaching it${on ? '' : ' (powered down: lightMeter.begin())'}`, `I2C 0x${addr.toString(16)}, ${reads} reads`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n// TCS34725: registers with the command bit (0x80): 0x00 ENABLE (bit 0 power, bit 1 measure),\n// 0x01 ATIME, 0x0F CONTROL (gain), 0x12 ID = 0x44, 0x13 STATUS (bit 0 valid), 0x14-0x1B C, R, G, B\n// (16-bit, low byte first). Its eye is a little camera looking out of its face.\nbench.device('tcs34725', (part) => {\n  const eye = part.camera('eye');\n  const regs = new Array(32).fill(0);\n  regs[0x12] = 0x44;\n  regs[0x01] = 0xff;\n  let powered = false, ptr = 0, reads = 0, led = true, rgb = [0, 0, 0], seen = false;\n  const GAINS = [1, 4, 16, 60];\n  return {\n    i2c: {\n      address: () => (powered ? 0x29 : -1),\n      write(bytes) {\n        if (!bytes.length) return true;\n        const cmd = bytes[0];\n        ptr = cmd & 0x1f;\n        for (let i = 1; i < bytes.length; i++) regs[(ptr + i - 1) & 31] = bytes[i];\n        return true;\n      },\n      read(n) {\n        reads++;\n        const out = [];\n        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(regs[(ptr + i) & 31]);\n        return out;\n      },\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      const v = io.supply('VIN', 'GND');\n      powered = v >= 2.7;\n      led = io.level('LED') !== 0;\n      const measuring = powered && (regs[0x00] & 3) === 3;\n      eye.want(measuring ? 10 : 0);\n      const f = eye.frame;\n      if (f) {\n        let r = 0, g = 0, b = 0;\n        for (let i = 0; i < f.width * f.height; i++) { r += f.data[i * 4]; g += f.data[i * 4 + 1]; b += f.data[i * 4 + 2]; }\n        const k = f.width * f.height * 255;\n        rgb = [r / k, g / k, b / k];\n        seen = true;\n      }\n      if (measuring) {\n        const cycles = 256 - regs[0x01];\n        const full = Math.min(65535, cycles * 1024);\n        const gain = GAINS[regs[0x0f] & 3];\n        // its LED lights what's in front of it; without it, only the room does (dimmer)\n        const lit = led ? 0.5 : 0.18;\n        const ch = rgb.map((x) => Math.min(65535, Math.round(Math.pow(x, 2.2) * full * gain * lit * 0.25)));\n        const c = Math.min(65535, ch[0] + ch[1] + ch[2]);\n        [c, ch[0], ch[1], ch[2]].forEach((val, i) => { regs[0x14 + i * 2] = val & 255; regs[0x15 + i * 2] = val >> 8; });\n        regs[0x13] |= 1;\n      }\n      io.draw(powered ? ((regs[0x00] & 1 ? 0.0002 : 0.000003) + (led ? 0.004 : 0)) : 0);\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\n      if ((regs[0x00] & 3) !== 3) return ['asleep (tcs.begin() wakes it)'];\n      if (!seen) return ['looking...'];\n      return [`sees r ${Math.round(rgb[0] * 255)} g ${Math.round(rgb[1] * 255)} b ${Math.round(rgb[2] * 255)}${led ? ', LED on' : ''}`, `${reads} reads`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"BH1750.h":{"classes":["BH1750"],"code":"// BH1750.h (claws' library): BH1750 lightMeter;  lightMeter.begin();  lightMeter.readLightLevel() (lux).\n//   Modes: BH1750::CONTINUOUS_HIGH_RES_MODE (the default), CONTINUOUS_LOW_RES_MODE, ONE_TIME_HIGH_RES_MODE ...\nclass BH1750 {\n  constructor(addr = 0x23) { this.addr = addr; this.mode = BH1750.CONTINUOUS_HIGH_RES_MODE; this.last = -1; }\n  _cmd(c) { Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(c); return Wire.endTransmission() === 0; }\n  begin(mode = BH1750.CONTINUOUS_HIGH_RES_MODE, addr, _wire) {\n    if (addr) this.addr = addr;\n    if (!this._cmd(0x01)) return false;\n    return this.configure(mode);\n  }\n  configure(mode) {\n    this.mode = mode;\n    const ok = this._cmd(mode);\n    delay((mode & 3) === 3 ? 24 : 180); // (the first measurement)\n    return ok;\n  }\n  setMTreg() { return true; }\n  measurementReady() { return true; }\n  readLightLevel() {\n    if ((this.mode & 0xf0) === 0x20) { this._cmd(this.mode); delay((this.mode & 3) === 3 ? 24 : 180); }\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.addr, 2) < 2) return -1;\n    const v = (Wire.read() << 8) | Wire.read();\n    this.last = v / 1.2;\n    return this.last;\n  }\n}\nBH1750.UNCONFIGURED = 0;\nBH1750.CONTINUOUS_HIGH_RES_MODE = 0x10;\nBH1750.CONTINUOUS_HIGH_RES_MODE_2 = 0x11;\nBH1750.CONTINUOUS_LOW_RES_MODE = 0x13;\nBH1750.ONE_TIME_HIGH_RES_MODE = 0x20;\nBH1750.ONE_TIME_HIGH_RES_MODE_2 = 0x21;\nBH1750.ONE_TIME_LOW_RES_MODE = 0x23;\n"},"Adafruit_TCS34725.h":{"classes":["Adafruit_TCS34725"],"exports":["TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_2_4MS","TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_24MS","TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_50MS","TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_101MS","TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_154MS","TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_614MS","TCS34725_GAIN_1X","TCS34725_GAIN_4X","TCS34725_GAIN_16X","TCS34725_GAIN_60X"],"code":"// Adafruit_TCS34725.h: Adafruit_TCS34725 tcs = Adafruit_TCS34725(TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_50MS, TCS34725_GAIN_4X);\n//   tcs.begin();  uint16_t r, g, b, c;  tcs.getRawData(&r, &g, &b, &c);  float R, G, B;  tcs.getRGB(&R, &G, &B);\n//   tcs.calculateColorTemperature_dn40(r, g, b, c);  tcs.calculateLux(r, g, b);  tcs.setInterrupt(true) (LED off)\nconst TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_2_4MS = 0xff, TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_24MS = 0xf6, TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_50MS = 0xeb;\nconst TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_101MS = 0xd5, TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_154MS = 0xc0, TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_614MS = 0x00;\nconst TCS34725_GAIN_1X = 0, TCS34725_GAIN_4X = 1, TCS34725_GAIN_16X = 2, TCS34725_GAIN_60X = 3;\n\nclass Adafruit_TCS34725 {\n  constructor(it = TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_2_4MS, gain = TCS34725_GAIN_1X) { this.it = it; this.gain = gain; this.addr = 0x29; this.ok = false; }\n  _w(reg, v) { Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(0x80 | reg); Wire.write(v); return Wire.endTransmission() === 0; }\n  _r(reg, n) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(0x80 | reg);\n    if (Wire.endTransmission() !== 0) return null;\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.addr, n) < n) return null;\n    const out = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(Wire.read());\n    return out;\n  }\n  begin(addr = 0x29) {\n    this.addr = addr;\n    const id = this._r(0x12, 1);\n    if (!id || (id[0] !== 0x44 && id[0] !== 0x4d && id[0] !== 0x10)) return false;\n    this.ok = true;\n    this.setIntegrationTime(this.it);\n    this.setGain(this.gain);\n    this.enable();\n    return true;\n  }\n  enable() { this._w(0x00, 0x01); delay(3); this._w(0x00, 0x03); delay(Math.ceil((256 - this.it) * 2.4)); }\n  disable() { this._w(0x00, 0x00); }\n  setIntegrationTime(it) { this.it = it; this._w(0x01, it); }\n  setGain(g) { this.gain = g; this._w(0x0f, g); }\n  /** fills r, g, b, c (handed over: getRawData(&r, &g, &b, &c)); returns them too */\n  getRawData(r, g, b, c) {\n    if (!this.ok) return [0, 0, 0, 0];\n    const d = this._r(0x14, 8) ?? new Array(8).fill(0);\n    const v = [0, 2, 4, 6].map((i) => d[i] | (d[i + 1] << 8));\n    setRef(c, v[0]); setRef(r, v[1]); setRef(g, v[2]); setRef(b, v[3]);\n    delay(Math.ceil((256 - this.it) * 2.4)); // (as the real one: it waits for a fresh reading)\n    return [v[1], v[2], v[3], v[0]];\n  }\n  getRawDataOneShot(r, g, b, c) { return this.getRawData(r, g, b, c); }\n  /** red, green, blue as 0-255 (scaled by the clear channel), into floats handed over */\n  getRGB(r, g, b) {\n    const [R, G, B, C] = this.getRawData(null, null, null, null);\n    const k = C ? 255 / C : 0;\n    setRef(r, R * k); setRef(g, G * k); setRef(b, B * k);\n  }\n  calculateColorTemperature(r, g, b) {\n    const X = -0.14282 * r + 1.54924 * g + -0.95641 * b, Y = -0.32466 * r + 1.57837 * g + -0.73191 * b, Z = -0.68202 * r + 0.77073 * g + 0.56332 * b;\n    const xc = X / (X + Y + Z), yc = Y / (X + Y + Z);\n    const n = (xc - 0.332) / (0.1858 - yc);\n    return Math.round(449.0 * n ** 3 + 3525.0 * n ** 2 + 6823.3 * n + 5520.33);\n  }\n  calculateColorTemperature_dn40(r, g, b, c) {\n    if (!c) return 0;\n    const ir = r + g + b > c ? (r + g + b - c) / 2 : 0;\n    const r2 = r - ir, b2 = b - ir;\n    if (r2 === 0) return 0;\n    return Math.round((3810 * b2) / r2 + 1391);\n  }\n  calculateLux(r, g, b) { return Math.round(-0.32466 * r + 1.57837 * g + -0.73191 * b); }\n  /** true: LED off (on the Adafruit board the INT pin drives it; here: wire LED to a pin instead) */\n  setInterrupt() {}\n  clearInterrupt() {}\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"ldr","name":"Light sensor module (LDR)","description":"A photoresistor with a comparator: AO rises as it gets darker (about 0.2 V in a lit room, near VCC in the dark), DO goes HIGH when it's darker than the blue pot's setting. VCC (3.3-5 V), GND, DO, AO. Switch the room dark (toolbar), or hold something over it.","swatch":"#1f5fbf","mass":2,"params":[{"key":"threshold","label":"Pot: dark below (lux)","kind":"number","min":1,"max":1000,"step":1}],"defaults":{"threshold":60},"shape":[{"box":[1.5,0.16,3.2],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1f5fbf"},{"cyl":[0.25,0.3],"at":[0,0.31,1.2],"color":"#c8a050"},{"box":[0.6,0.4,0.6],"at":[0.3,0.36,-0.2],"color":"#3a70e0"},{"light":{"id":"eye","look":[0,1,0],"fov":120},"at":[0,0.5,1.2]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VCC","GND","DO","AO"],"at":[-0.381,0,-1.45],"kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","DO":"out","AO":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2.5,"vmax":5.5},"DO":{"label":"DO (HIGH = dark)"},"AO":{"label":"AO (higher = darker)","analog":true}}}],"device":"ldr"},{"id":"bh1750","name":"Light meter (BH1750)","description":"Measures light in lux (I2C at 0x23, or 0x5C with ADDR high). VCC (3.3-5 V), GND, SCL, SDA. #include <BH1750.h>; BH1750 lightMeter; lightMeter.begin(); lightMeter.readLightLevel().","swatch":"#1f5fbf","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[1.4,0.16,1.9],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1f5fbf"},{"box":[0.35,0.12,0.25],"at":[0,0.22,0.4],"color":"#141416"},{"light":{"id":"eye","look":[0,1,0],"fov":120},"at":[0,0.35,0.4]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VCC","GND","SCL","SDA","ADDR"],"at":[-0.508,0,-0.8],"kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","SCL":"i2c","SDA":"i2c","ADDR":"in"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2.4,"vmax":5.5},"ADDR":{"pulled":"down"}}}],"device":"bh1750"},{"id":"tcs34725","name":"Colour sensor (TCS34725)","description":"Sees the colour of what's in front of its face (a few cm), lit by its white LED (LED pin: HIGH or unwired = on). I2C at 0x29. VIN (3.3-5 V), GND, SCL, SDA, LED. #include <Adafruit_TCS34725.h>; tcs.begin(); tcs.getRawData(&r, &g, &b, &c); or tcs.getRGB(&r, &g, &b). Glue it face down over where things pass.","swatch":"#2a2d8f","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[2,0.16,2],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#2a2d8f"},{"box":[0.3,0.1,0.3],"at":[0,0.21,0.2],"color":"#e8e8e8"},{"box":[0.3,0.12,0.3],"at":[0.55,0.22,0.2],"color":"#ffffff","collide":false},{"camera":{"id":"eye","px":[8,8],"fov":50,"look":[0,1,0],"range":12},"at":[0,0.3,0.2]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["LED","INT","SDA","SCL","GND","VIN"],"at":[-0.635,0,-0.8],"kinds":{"LED":"in","INT":"out","SDA":"i2c","SCL":"i2c","GND":"gnd","VIN":"vin"},"extra":{"VIN":{"label":"VIN (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2.7,"vmax":5.5},"LED":{"pulled":"up"}}}],"device":"tcs34725"}],"examples":[{"name":"Night light","description":"An LED that comes on when it gets dark, and a light meter printing lux. Press Run, then press the toolbar's Room button to dim the room (or hold something over the sensors: drag a block over them).","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Night light","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-10,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"ldr","type":"light-sensors/ldr","name":"Light sensor","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[3,0,-4],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"meter","type":"light-sensors/bh1750","name":"Light meter","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[3,0,5],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"led","type":"led","name":"Night light","params":{"color":"white"},"parent":null,"pos":[-10,0,8],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"cover","type":"block","name":"Box (drag it over a sensor)","params":{"w":5,"h":3,"d":5,"material":"cardboard","color":"#b98b55"},"parent":null,"pos":[12,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"ldr","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"ldr","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"ldr","pin":"DO"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"A0"},"b":{"uid":"ldr","pin":"AO"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"meter","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"meter","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SDA"},"b":{"uid":"meter","pin":"SDA"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SCL"},"b":{"uid":"meter","pin":"SCL"},"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"led","pin":"A"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"led","pin":"K"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Night light: the LED comes on when the light sensor says it's dark. Press the toolbar's Room\n// button to dim the room, or drag the box over the sensor. The light meter prints lux (Plot them).\n#include <Wire.h>\n#include <BH1750.h>\n\n#define DARK 2      // the LDR module's DO: HIGH when dark\n#define LEVEL A0    // its AO: higher when darker\n#define LAMP 15\n\nBH1750 meter;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  Wire.begin();\n  meter.begin();\n  pinMode(DARK, INPUT);\n  pinMode(LAMP, OUTPUT);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  bool dark = digitalRead(DARK) == HIGH;\n  digitalWrite(LAMP, dark ? HIGH : LOW);\n  float lux = meter.readLightLevel();\n  Serial.print(\"lux:\");\n  Serial.print(lux, 0);\n  Serial.print(\" ldr:\");\n  Serial.println(analogRead(LEVEL));\n  delay(400);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"Colour names","description":"A colour sensor on an arm looks down at what's under it and prints the colour's name. Drag the coloured blocks under it one by one.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Colour names","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-14,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"post","type":"block","name":"Post","params":{"w":2,"h":6,"d":2,"material":"wood","color":"#c98a4b"},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,-6],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"arm","type":"block","name":"Arm","params":{"w":2,"h":1,"d":8,"material":"wood","color":"#c98a4b"},"parent":{"uid":"post","body":"body"},"pos":[0,6,3],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"tcs","type":"light-sensors/tcs34725","name":"Colour sensor","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"arm","body":"body"},"pos":[0,0,3],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"paper","type":"plate","name":"White paper","params":{"w":16,"h":0.3,"d":14,"material":"cardboard","color":"#f4f4f2"},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"bred","type":"block","name":"Red block","params":{"w":3.5,"h":2.5,"d":3.5,"material":"plastic","color":"#d02020"},"parent":null,"pos":[12,0,4],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"bgreen","type":"block","name":"Green block","params":{"w":3.5,"h":2.5,"d":3.5,"material":"plastic","color":"#20a040"},"parent":null,"pos":[17,0,4],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"bblue","type":"block","name":"Blue block","params":{"w":3.5,"h":2.5,"d":3.5,"material":"plastic","color":"#2050d0"},"parent":null,"pos":[22,0,4],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"byellow","type":"block","name":"Yellow block","params":{"w":3.5,"h":2.5,"d":3.5,"material":"plastic","color":"#e8c820"},"parent":null,"pos":[27,0,4],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"bwhite","type":"block","name":"White block","params":{"w":3.5,"h":2.5,"d":3.5,"material":"plastic","color":"#f2f2f2"},"parent":null,"pos":[32,0,4],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"tcs","pin":"VIN"},"color":"#e04848","length":30},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"tcs","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33","length":30},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SDA"},"b":{"uid":"tcs","pin":"SDA"},"color":"#3cb371","length":30},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SCL"},"b":{"uid":"tcs","pin":"SCL"},"color":"#f2f2f2","length":30}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Colour names: the TCS34725 looks down from the arm at the white paper. Drag a coloured block\n// under it.\n#include <Wire.h>\n#include <Adafruit_TCS34725.h>\n\nAdafruit_TCS34725 tcs = Adafruit_TCS34725(TCS34725_INTEGRATIONTIME_50MS, TCS34725_GAIN_4X);\n\nString nameOf(float r, float g, float b, uint16_t c) {\n  if (c < 300) return \"nothing (too dark)\";\n  if (r > 0.33 && g > 0.33 && b < 0.25) return \"yellow\";   // (red and green together, little blue)\n  if (r > 0.27 && g > 0.27 && b > 0.27 && max(r, max(g, b)) < 0.42) return \"white (just the paper?)\";\n  if (r > g && r > b) return \"red\";\n  if (g > r && g > b) return \"green\";\n  return \"blue\";\n}\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  Wire.begin();\n  if (!tcs.begin()) {\n    Serial.println(\"No TCS34725: check its wires\");\n    while (true) delay(100);\n  }\n}\n\nString last = \"\";\n\nvoid loop() {\n  uint16_t r, g, b, c;\n  tcs.getRawData(&r, &g, &b, &c);\n  float sum = r + g + b;\n  if (sum < 1) sum = 1;\n  String name = nameOf(r / sum, g / sum, b / sum, c);\n  if (name != last) {\n    Serial.print(\"I see \");\n    Serial.print(name);\n    Serial.print(\"  (r \");\n    Serial.print(r);\n    Serial.print(\", g \");\n    Serial.print(g);\n    Serial.print(\", b \");\n    Serial.print(b);\n    Serial.println(\")\");\n    last = name;\n  }\n  delay(200);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}